al security  ambassador bolton says  china is the biggest existential threat  to western democracies  like canada we'll have more of that on  the show as well as an exclusive  one-on-one interview with seniors  minister deb schult  i had many questions on the federal  government's supports for seniors  particularly during the kovig 19  pandemic  are you concerned about seniors mental  health absolutely i mean the second wave  you just think  your heart breaks for these folks who  are in long-term care homes  it's emotional for me too can see it in  your eyes you have dementia  i mean i'll tell you why because i had  my mother-in-law  in a long-term care facility and she  passed away in june  so i am totally aware of the challenges  that families have had across canada  i've got my father-in-law in a senior's  residence and the challenges that he has  with us not being able to see him and  and the mental health  uh the strain of him losing his wife not  being able to see her  as she deteriorated because we weren't  able to be with her  so it is very emotional i'm emotional  too because i've i've  i've lived it and um and i hear the  stories and i'm on the phone  and i got the emails and i'm with people  every day that are struggling with this  issue and robin we did not forget about  that confidence motion we saw in the  house that almost triggered an election  political strategists of all stripes  join us to unpack  exactly how canada avoided a snap  election  all that and more is coming up on this  week's the west walk  robin all right mercedes stevenson in  ottawa  a sad end to the search for a missing  new brunswick man who was a well-known  writer in the province's arts community  police in fredericton confirmed the body  of richard vaughn has been located  ten days after he was reported missing  he was last seen near his home on  thanksgiving  he was an author a playwright and poet  under the name  r.m vaughan and he served as the writer  in residence at the university of new  brunswick  friends and colleagues have also  described him as a mentor in the lgbtq2  community  von's death is not being treated as  suspicious he was 55.  still ahead the protest over a ban on  abortion in a country that  already has strict laws  you're watching global national  poland's president has tested positive  for covid19  in a country that reported more than 13  000 cases and 179 deaths  today andre duda has apologized to his  close contacts  who are being told to isolate the 48  year old says he has no symptoms  and is feeling good poland's president  joins a handful of world leaders who've  contracted covet 19  including the american president and  british prime minister  and tension is growing in poland tonight  over a new ban on abortions  thousands of demonstrators marched  across the country for a third straight  day of protests  on thursday poland's highest court ruled  that having an abortion  because of a defect was unconstitutional  the nation which already had some of the  strictest abortion laws in europe  will now only allow the procedure in  cases of rape  incest or when the mother's life is in  danger  the death toll from a suicide bomb  attack in the afghan capital  is expected to rise as crews dig through  debris  the explosion happened yesterday  afternoon at an education center in  kabul  in a predominantly shiite neighborhood  the attacker was trying to enter the  center when he was stopped by security  at least 18 people are dead and 57  others injured  but many families are still desperately  searching for their loved ones  up next the food fight over uk holidays  and school meals  hunger is a growing issue when school  breaks for holiday in the uk  students miss out on free meals provided  during school and families facing food  and security  rely on these programs to feed their  kids but the government blocked one  british athlete's attempt to extend the  program over school holidays  as crystal gomencing reports that has  sparked outrage  and compassion  it's nothing fancy just a sandwich  but it could be enough to stop a little  stomach  from rumbling i've been watching the  news and watching these stories and it's  been really sad  so i just thought right i'm going to  spend some money and feed some children  it's as simple as that ali waterworth  runs a children's charity  and cafe like many she was shocked when  boris johnson's government  voted down a labour party motion to  extend the school meals program  and offer families vouchers over the  half-term break  the government after all had seen the  value in extending it over the summer  months  saying families were battling added  pressures with the pandemic  it leaves me speechless if i'm honest  boris has got other things on his mind  at the minute and he's not doing it  as he should by the kids in my opinion  soccer star and poverty advocate  marcus rashford championed that  summertime meal program extension  he grew up in manchester and remembers  being hungry as a boy  despite having a hard-working loving mom  in rejecting this latest extension some  tory mps said it would create a  dependency on the state  and that the primary responsibility for  child welfare  rests with parents i know for sure that  a lot of them speak in the way that  they're speaking it's so insensitive  about the issue  and they've definitely not not been  through it themselves rashford and his  mom spent some time at a food share  food distribution center all the while  keeping up with his  online plea to feed hungry children  which led to this the young man's  twitter page now  reads like a giant takeout menu it is  filled with generous offers from little  shop owners to local town  councils all pledging to not let any  child  go hungry and then there are dozens of  tweets  reacting to the outpouring of kindness  the mayor of london  shared this post if you need a reminding  that our country is far  better and more generous than this  government  have a look at marcus rashford's twitter  feed this morning  as donations and accolades pour in  rashford watched his mom who once needed  help feeding her children  honored by having a food share warehouse  named after her  a moment to savor but not rest  rashford pledges to keep fighting and  giving a voice to those  who are struggling crystal gamson global  news  london and that is global national for  this saturday  i'm robin gill tonight your canada is  the early snowfall in prince george bc  we'd love to see your corner of this  country so please send your photos  to viewers at globalnational.com thank  you for watching and i'll see you back  here tomorrow  have a great night  [Music]
 

